<title>GERMANY: Stinnes buys Krupp steel trade unit.</title>
<headline>Stinnes buys Krupp steel trade unit.</headline>
<dateline>MUELHEIM, Germany 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stinnes AG, a trading unit of utilities conglomerate Veba AG, said it would buy Krupp-Hoesch Stahl's steel trading unit.  </p>
<p>Stinnes will integrate Krupp Hoesch Stahlhandel in its Stinnes Interfer unit, the largest independent steel vendor in Germany with sales of two billion marks a year.</p>
<p>The purchase covers Krupp facilities in Bremen, Hamburg, Bielefeld, Isernhagen, Dortmund and Frankfurt with 370 employees. Krupp Hoesch Stahlhandel has annual sales of about 465 million marks, or 455,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
